{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' .head-developer/MEGAPLAN.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Megaplan\n> Generated by the Megaplan skill. Approval is required before the local Codex CLI implementation session starts.\n## Approval Gate\n- Status: Pending user approval\n- To start: reply `approve` in the Codex chat\n- To revise: describe the change before approving\n## Repository\n- Repo: Codexa Smoke Quote Board 3\n- Repo URL: [https://github.com/MeharPro/voice-agent-hackathon.git](https://github.com/MeharPro/voice-agent-hackathon.git)\n- Branch: main\n- Commit: 34c4441\n- Local path: `/Users/meharkhanna/Documents/voice-agent-hackathon/codexa-workspace/generated-projects/codexa-smoke-quote-board-3`\n## User Request\nPlan a tiny static quote board app with saved favorite quotes. Use GPT-5.5 low planning and ask for approval before implementation.\n## Requirement Summary\nBuild a tiny static quote board app named codexa-smoke-quote-board-3 with saved favorite quotes, using GPT-5.5 low planning. Implementation must wait for approval. Static local app only, with favorites persisted in browser localStorage.\n## Technical Requirements\n- Architecture/product scope: A small static quote board with seeded quotes displayed as cards, favorite toggle controls, a favorites-only view or filter, empty-state messaging, responsive styling, and localStorage persistence for favorite quote IDs. Include `.head-developer/IMPROVEMENTS.md` for deferred observations and avoid scope-changing improvements without approval.\n- Assumption: The app is static HTML/CSS/JavaScript, not a full-stack app.\n- Assumption: Favorite quotes are persisted in browser localStorage.\n- Assumption: No authentication, backend API, database, payments, deployment, or external quote API is required.\n- Assumption: A single local Codex CLI session in the current repo is sufficient.\n- Local validation expected: test -f .head-developer/PROJECT_BRIEF.md; test -f .head-developer/TASK_GRAPH.md; test -f .head-developer/IMPROVEMENTS.md; test -f index.html; test -f styles.css; test -f script.js; node --check script.js\n## Proposed Product Direction\nA small static quote board with seeded quotes displayed as cards, favorite toggle controls, a favorites-only view or filter, empty-state messaging, responsive styling, and localStorage persistence for favorite quote IDs. Include `.head-developer/IMPROVEMENTS.md` for deferred observations and avoid scope-changing improvements without approval.\n## Codex Orchestration\n- One local Codex CLI session owns the repo.\n- Codex decides how many internal subagents are useful; for non-trivial work it should prefer visible named responsibility lanes when that is truthful.\n- Subagents are logical Codex responsibilities, not Docker, VM, GKE, or cloud workers.\n- The user can revise subagent use before approval; approval permits Codex to choose the actual internal count and names.\n- If Codex later determines a materially different subagent strategy is needed, it must stop and ask before changing scope, cost, risk, or timeline.\n- The browser flowchart updates rapidly from a parallel Codex flowchart process and shows only the subagents Codex actually reports.\n## Subagent Check-In\n- Advisor recommendation: single-lane Codex run is acceptable.\n- Reason: The Codex planner produced a narrow responsibility split, so a direct implementation lane looks sufficient.\n- User check-in: The plan looks narrow enough for a direct Codex lane. Approval keeps Codex free to ask before changing to a materially different subagent strategy.\n- Likely responsibility areas: Build static app\n- Advisor source: planner_context\n## Continuous Improvement Loop\n- Codex should look for bugs, UX gaps, performance issues, maintainability problems, missing tests, and feature opportunities while implementing.\n- Codex may implement improvements that fit the approved plan or are required for correctness,